  "description": "EQEDEM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C145 H157 Br10 Cd6 N15 O50 Tb4 4+,4(N1 O3 1-),C1 H2 Cl2,2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Cd1 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Cd2 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Cd3 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Cd4 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Cd5 (Cd) has 3 O neighbors; Cd6 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Cd7? (Cd) has 0 O neighbors; Cd8? (Cd) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 6 components; largest component is a chain with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.640-4.173 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.89-111.83°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C148H165Br10Cd6Cl2N19O64Tb4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
